{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2186-06-16 07:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning, Ms. ___. I’m Dr. ___, part of the breast surgery team. You’re here today for your scheduled left total mastectomy due to recurrent breast cancer. How are you feeling this morning?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2186-06-16 07:16:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Hi, Doctor. I’m a little nervous, but I’m ready to get this done. I’ve been through this before, so I know what to expect, more or less."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2186-06-16 07:18:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s completely understandable. You’ve had a lumpectomy and radiation before, correct? And no signs of recurrence until now?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2186-06-16 07:19:20",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, that’s right. It was over ten years ago. I’ve been followed closely, and then this new mass showed up on my mammogram."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2186-06-16 07:20:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, the imaging showed a new spiculated mass in the upper inner quadrant. The biopsy confirmed invasive lobular carcinoma, grade 2. The good news is it’s ER and PR positive, which gives us good treatment options later."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2186-06-16 07:22:10",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And HER2 negative, right? That’s what my oncologist said."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2186-06-16 07:23:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Correct. HER2 negative. That means we won’t use drugs like Herceptin, but hormone therapy will likely be part of your plan after surgery."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2186-06-16 07:24:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, that makes sense. I’ve been on tamoxifen before. Will I go back on something like that?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2186-06-16 07:25:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Possibly. Your medical oncologist will decide that after reviewing the final pathology. For now, we’re proceeding with the mastectomy. We discussed skipping the sentinel lymph node biopsy—does that still sound okay to you?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2186-06-16 07:26:50",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes. Since I already had the full node dissection and radiation, it seems unnecessary to do it again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2186-06-16 07:27:40",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. The tumor board agreed. It wouldn’t change treatment decisions, and it adds risk without benefit in your case."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2186-06-16 07:28:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good. I also wanted to mention—I had a little accident last week in the pool."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2186-06-16 07:29:20",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, I saw that in your history. You hit your chest and abdomen getting out?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2186-06-16 07:30:10",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes. No broken bones, but my GJ tube site has been a bit sore. It doesn’t sit as flush as before."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2186-06-16 07:31:20",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll keep an eye on that. The surgical site is on the left, and your GJ tube is on the abdomen, so they’re separate. But we’ll make sure your gastroparesis is managed carefully—no heavy narcotics that could slow things further."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2186-06-16 07:32:40",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m used to that. I take Reglan and Zofran at home. Will I be able to restart those soon?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2186-06-16 07:33:50",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes. We’ll start clear liquids once you’re awake and then advance as tolerated. We’ll restart your meds as soon as you can take them by mouth."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2186-06-16 07:35:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my thyroid and anxiety meds too?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2186-06-16 07:35:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Absolutely. All your regular medications will be resumed unless there’s a specific reason not to. We’ve got your list: Celexa, Synthroid, lorazepam, gabapentin, omeprazole."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2186-06-16 07:37:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you. I get anxious if I miss my lorazepam at night."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2186-06-16 07:38:10",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll make sure you get it. Now, the surgery should take about two hours. You’ll wake up in the PACU with a drain in place to collect fluid from the surgical site."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2186-06-16 07:39:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "One drain? Last time I had two."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2186-06-16 07:40:20",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "This time, one should be enough. We’ll monitor the output. Once it drops below 30 cc per day for two days, we can remove it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2186-06-16 07:41:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. And I’ll have help with it at home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2186-06-16 07:42:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, visiting nurse services will come to assist with drain care and check your incision. You’ll also have a follow-up appointment in one week."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2186-06-16 07:43:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good. I live alone, so that helps."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2186-06-16 07:44:20",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll make sure you’re not alone in this. Any other questions before we head to the OR?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2186-06-16 07:45:10",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No, I think I’m ready. Thank you for explaining everything."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2186-06-16 13:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Ms. ___, welcome back. The surgery went very well. You’ve had a left total mastectomy, and the incision looks clean. You have one JP drain in place, and your vitals are stable."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2186-06-16 13:01:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "How do I feel? Sore, but okay. Is the drain hurting?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2186-06-16 13:02:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It might feel a little tugging, but we’ve given you acetaminophen and tramadol for pain. We’re avoiding strong narcotics because of your gastroparesis."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2186-06-16 13:04:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Smart. Morphine really slows me down."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2186-06-16 13:05:10",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. We want you up and moving to prevent complications. You’ll wear compression sleeves and use the incentive spirometer every hour while awake."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2186-06-16 13:06:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I remember that from last time. Deep breaths to keep my lungs clear."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2186-06-16 13:07:20",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes. And we’ll start you on clear liquids soon—water, broth. If you tolerate that, we’ll move to a regular diet tomorrow."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2186-06-16 13:08:40",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Can I have my Reglan and Zofran tonight?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2186-06-16 13:09:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Once you’re tolerating liquids, yes. We’ll start them this evening."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2186-06-17 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. You did great overnight. You’re afebrile, pain is controlled, and you’ve been eating a regular diet. We’re planning to discharge you today."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2186-06-17 09:01:20",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s great. What do I need to do at home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2186-06-17 09:02:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll remove the dressing in 48 hours and keep the incision open to air. Clean around the drain site with soap and water, empty the bulb twice daily, and record the output."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2186-06-17 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And no lifting?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2186-06-17 09:04:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Nothing heavier than five pounds for two weeks. No driving while on tramadol. And call us if you have fever, increased redness, or severe pain."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2186-06-17 09:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "What about my GJ tube? Should I be worried about the discomfort?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2186-06-17 09:07:10",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It’s likely just bruising from the fall. Keep the site clean. If it becomes red, swollen, or starts draining, call your GI doctor."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2186-06-17 09:08:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. And my follow-up is in one week?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2186-06-17 09:09:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, and the visiting nurse will help until then. You’re doing really well, Ms. ___."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2186-06-17 09:10:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you, Doctor. I feel lucky to have such a good team."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2186-06-17 09:11:40",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re glad to take care of you. Let’s get your discharge papers ready."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2186-06-17 10:30:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "One last thing—will I need chemotherapy?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2186-06-17 10:31:20",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That decision will be made by your oncologist based on the final pathology. Since it’s ER/PR positive and HER2 negative, hormone therapy is likely, but chemo may not be needed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2186-06-17 10:32:40",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I hope not. I really didn’t tolerate it well last time."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2186-06-17 10:33:50",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll discuss all options at your follow-up. For now, focus on healing."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 53,
      "time": "2186-06-17 11:00:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m ready to go home. Thank you again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 54,
      "time": "2186-06-17 11:01:10",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Remember—rest, follow the instructions, and we’ll see you next week."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 55,
      "time": "2186-06-17 11:02:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. Take care."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 56,
      "time": "2186-06-17 11:03:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You too. Have a safe trip home."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2186-06-16 07:15:00",
    "admission_end": "2186-06-17 13:40:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A woman with a history of breast cancer, gastroparesis, and a GJ tube presented for a left total mastectomy due to recurrent invasive lobular carcinoma in the upper-inner quadrant, ER/PR positive and HER2 negative. The surgery was uncomplicated, and she was admitted for overnight observation. Pain was managed with acetaminophen and tramadol to avoid exacerbating gastroparesis. She tolerated a clear diet postoperatively and advanced to a regular diet, remained afebrile, and was ambulating well. A single JP drain was placed, and visiting nurse services were arranged for home care. She was discharged on postoperative day one with instructions for wound and drain care, activity restrictions, and a follow-up appointment in one week. Final pathology is pending, and further oncologic treatment will be determined in consultation with medical oncology.",
    "problems": [
      "Malignant neoplasm of upper-inner quadrant of left female breast",
      "Estrogen receptor positive status [ER+]",
      "Gastroparesis",
      "Other artificial openings of gastrointestinal tract status",
      "Adhesive capsulitis of right shoulder",
      "Dorsalgia, unspecified",
      "Age-related osteoporosis without current pathological fracture",
      "Hypothyroidism, unspecified",
      "Gastro-esophageal reflux disease without esophagitis",
      "Iron deficiency anemia, unspecified",
      "Anxiety disorder, unspecified",
      "Major depressive disorder, single episode, unspecified",
      "Family history of malignant neoplasm of digestive organs"
    ]
  }
}
